content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-201 — Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Diaphragm/head leakage is approximately 2 drops per second, representing active chemical loss of containment. No Velatek VX-90 allowable leakage rate or leak-based running/shutdown limit is supplied, so this reading cannot be classified against an applicable manufacturer limit. C09 concerns AquaDyne HF-300 shaft-seal leakage and is neither a diaphragm-leak limit nor applicable to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The motor is reported only as 'running normally'; no speed, current, temperature or vibration reading is available. The HF-300 bearing-housing temperature limits—normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C—and the HF-300 vibration severity zones do not apply to the Velatek VX-90. No applicable VX-90 motor limit comparison can therefore be made.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P1 and immediate controlled shutdown are conservative work-order decisions for the active chemical leak, not a claim that an HF-300 temperature or vibration trip limit was exceeded. SSP-07's specific priority-1 trigger for bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit cannot be evaluated because neither an applicable VX-90 alarm limit nor a bearing-temperature reading is provided.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Shut down P-201 for the active chemical leak. Before opening the pump head or performing any other work inside the pump, electrically isolate it and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; SSP-07 applies to all pumps on site.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Drain and vent first, then obtain the required line-break permit before opening the chemically wetted pump head or line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not use the AquaDyne HF-300 mechanical-seal troubleshooting or replacement procedure, its fastener torques, or its service-bulletin parts for this repair. Hold the disassembly, repair and reassembly specification pending the correct Velatek VX-90 instructions for serial VX-5531; then add the model-specific steps, inspection criteria and torque values to this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not restart or return the pump to service until the correct VX-90 repair and leakage acceptance criteria have been obtained and the repair scope has been confirmed. The supplied HF-300 documents provide no applicable VX-90 restart criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For work on the chemically dosed line, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Do not identify the chemical as sodium hypochlorite from C16: that chunk applies only to filtered-water pumps P-101 through P-106, not P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional lifting control: if any component to be lifted is heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The 68 kg back-pull-out assembly mass in C02 is for the AquaDyne HF-300 and must not be assumed to be the mass of any P-201 component.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "No labour hours or crew size are assigned. C12 lists 4.0 hours with two technicians for HF-300 mechanical-seal replacement, but that task and estimate do not apply to a Velatek VX-90 diaphragm/head repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque and seal selection conflict: the HF-300 manual Table 5 specifies 25 Nm, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, specifies HF3-450B and 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; pumps below that serial remain on HF3-450 and the manual Table 5. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90 with serial VX-5531, not an HF-300 and not within the bulletin serial range. Therefore neither torque, neither seal part number, nor the bulletin's HF3-455 sleeve-scoring criterion applies to this asset. No gland or head-fastener torque is specified in this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Document applicability decision: the AquaDyne operating manual and bulletin describe the HF-300, whereas the reported asset is a Velatek VX-90. Its mechanical-seal procedure, exploded back-pull-out assembly, parts, torques, labour times, temperature limits and vibration zones are consequently excluded from the P-201 repair specification. Only the site-wide SSP-07 controls are applied, because that procedure expressly covers all site pumps.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C04",
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C12",
        "C13",
        "C14"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Obtain the Velatek VX-90 manual, parts drawing and service instructions applicable to serial VX-5531. What is the model-specific diagnostic procedure, root cause, repair sequence, exact diaphragm/head bill of materials, fastener torque schedule, and test/restart criterion? The supplied AquaDyne HF-300 material cannot answer these points (C04, C09, C10, C11, C13).",
    "Which chemical is P-201 dosing, at what concentration, and what additional SDS, exposure-control, spill-response, drainage/disposal and PPE requirements apply? C16 identifies sodium hypochlorite only for P-101 to P-106; SSP-07 supplies goggles and nitrile gloves for chemically dosed-line work but does not identify P-201's chemical (C15, C16).",
    "What is the Velatek/site allowable diaphragm leakage rate, continued-running limit and post-repair leakage acceptance criterion for the reported 2 drops per second? No applicable VX-90 limit is present, and C09 is an HF-300 shaft-seal troubleshooting entry rather than a leak-rate limit (C09).",
    "What are the actual masses and lift requirements of any P-201 components that must be removed? Confirm whether the greater-than-25 kg lifting control is triggered; the 68 kg HF-300 assembly mass is not transferable to this pump (C02, C15).",
    "What model-specific labour allowance and technician crew are required after the repair scope is known? The HF-300 mechanical-seal allowance must not be used for this diaphragm/head repair (C12).",
    "Confirm the site priority and any chemical-release emergency-response escalation with operations. SSP-07 documents a priority-1 rule for bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm and an immediate-stop rule for the manufacturer's highest vibration zone, but no chemical-leak priority rule or applicable P-201 temperature/vibration assessment is supplied (C15)."
  ]
}
